  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "'Brocade' is another of the very fine red dissectums and is similar to 'Ornatum'. The differences in many of the to a green red and bronze later in the summer. It is a pleasant bronzing, not as harsh as some other cultivars. Fall coloration is usually bright red to crimson blended softly with orange. The multidissected sevenor ninelobed leaves are of medium size, 6-10 cm long and at least as wide. This form cascades and eventually makes a large rounded bush 3 m high and 3.5 m wide."
  },
